WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:05.460
Nothing improves in life unless you inspect
it regularly.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.009
And I mean nothing.

00:00:07.009 --> 00:00:08.630
So take any area of your life.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:09.920
For me, I'll give you an example.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.830
90 days ago I did not like where I was at
with my body weight, and my energy.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:18.910
I weighed 257 pounds and I've never weight
257 pounds.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:19.910
Ever.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:20.910
I went to a doctor.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.260
We spent four hours together.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.820
We did testing.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.990
We got every single thing I can get on myself.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:31.949
My body fat percentage, my body mass index,
water, how much fat my body carries, what

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:39.299
muscles do I need to have, triglycerides,
every single detail we could possibly do.

00:00:39.299 --> 00:00:40.299
He made the recommendations.

00:00:40.299 --> 00:00:41.730
The recommendations were made.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.690
I'm supposed to implement with the recommendations
that were made.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:49.110
So whatever those recommendations were, no
grains, you know, all this other stuff that

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:50.110
I went through.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.110
Fast forward 90 days later.

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.729
I went this morning.

00:00:52.729 --> 00:00:54.800
I ended up losing 24 pounds.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.200
I'm at 233 right now.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.080
I haven't weighed 233 since 2006.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.500
My energy is just off the charts.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.500
Why?

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.680
Because I inspected it.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.600
If I don't inspect it, that's not going to
happen.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.150
The same goes with your relationships.

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.440
The same goes with your business.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:10.460
The same goes with your life.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.330
The same goes with your finances.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:16.050
Back in the day in 2003, my credit score was
terrible.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:20.250
Every single month, I mean every single month,
I started running my credit score.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:23.930
Every month, on the 19th of the month, I ran
my credit score.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:27.500
Every month I read all my reports and found
out what wasn't supposed to be on there and

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.500
what was.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.740
A year, two years, three years later my credit
score went from a 489 to 822.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:33.740
Why?

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:34.740
Again, inspecting.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.320
So today I'm going to talk about how to inspect
your business.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.120
Again, this question is probably one of the
most common comments we get.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.080
Pat, how do you inspect your business?

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.820
Now prior to me getting into this, I want
to tell you that I've got a surprise for you

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:50.930
at the end, because this actually requires
you to have a PDF to print out and have access

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:54.580
to, so stay tuned and watch the entire video
because you do want to have this PDF to do

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:57.890
exactly with your own business, that I'll
tell you how I do it myself.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.810
It's a very, very extensive PDF that will
help you out with.

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:03.190
So, inspecting your business - how often do
I do this?

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:07.909
I do this, full day, once a year.

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:12.170
And another time per year, every six months
or so, I'll do it for a half a day.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:15.200
We'll sit down and go through a few things
on what we need to improve in, and we'll improve

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.200
it.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.850
But once a year, when I inspect this, is a
full day.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:21.580
Maybe two days, that we'll inspect the business.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:25.950
And it's multiple businesses, and it's multiple
parts of my life, when I'm doing my life planning

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.410
and business planning.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:28.410
So let's get right into it.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.450
How to inspect your business.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:33.349
First of all, there are 12 different categories
that I have here.

00:02:33.349 --> 00:02:37.670
And every one of them is tied to a number
and a goal.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:38.670
Every single one of them.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:43.440
So you see on the left side here is numbers
and goals, and then here is a different category

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.280
to inspect within your business.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:47.840
I'll explain every single one of them to you
and I'll tell you how I do this.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.840
#1: Team

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:49.840
The first one is team.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:50.840
What is a team?

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:57.190
So when I look at my team, who do I need,
who am I missing, what department needs help,

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:02.560
what department needs a leader, what department
needs support, what department doesn't need

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:07.319
people, what department do I need to fire
the weakest link that slows everybody else

00:03:07.319 --> 00:03:08.319
down.

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:10.340
But I look at the team within different departments.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:16.290
When I look at my team, I score the team,
between 0 to 10, how good do you feel about

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.290
your team.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.130
And by the way, you can score teams and getting
even more detail.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:25.600
You team could be your assistant, your team
could be could be your executives, your sales

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.660
force, it can be many different things.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:28.890
But I score my team.

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:32.610
Then once I score my team, I write the good,
bad, ugly.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.180
So let's just say the score is five.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:39.379
I write the good is that these two people
have grown a lot from last year to this year.

00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:40.920
And I'll put two names down.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:45.280
The bad is, we still don't have somebody that
knows how to do.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:49.849
. . The ugly is this one department is a disaster
this year.

00:03:49.849 --> 00:03:51.900
We've got to do something about this department.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:52.900
Great.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:57.599
Then in this category, I write my three actionable
items.

00:03:57.599 --> 00:03:58.599
So what am I going to be doing?

00:03:58.599 --> 00:04:01.800
I'm going to do this, I'm going to do that,
I'm going to do this.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:05.590
Now, this is tied to numbers and goals.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:09.160
So my goal is to hire three people, two in
this department, one in this department, fire

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:10.170
this person.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.810
Number, goal.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:16.879
Number two, my number that I'm going to do,
my expectation of this team is for them to

00:04:16.879 --> 00:04:21.519
do $600,000 in the next two weeks, whatever
the number may be for your business.

00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:22.519
Great.

00:04:22.519 --> 00:04:23.519
There's a goal.

00:04:23.519 --> 00:04:27.659
So every box will have a number and a goal
tied to it when it comes down to actionable

00:04:27.659 --> 00:04:28.659
items.

00:04:28.659 --> 00:04:29.659
#2: Sales Flow

00:04:29.659 --> 00:04:30.659
The second one is sales flow.

00:04:30.659 --> 00:04:33.240
How's my sales flow looking?

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.270
So I'll go through and look at the sales cycle,
right?

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:37.430
Where does the customer come in?

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:39.770
Once the customer comes in, what options do
they have?

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:42.610
Is it pretty easy for them to know what next
steps to take?

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:44.349
Do they find this pretty well?

00:04:44.349 --> 00:04:47.199
Do we do a good job of selling and do we do
a good job of presenting?

00:04:47.199 --> 00:04:51.610
Do we do a good job of going through the sales
flow part.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:54.319
Do the people know the products that they're
selling to them?

00:04:54.319 --> 00:04:55.379
It is pretty easy?

00:04:55.379 --> 00:04:56.539
Do we sell it in a simple way?

00:04:56.539 --> 00:04:57.669
Can it be found easy?

00:04:57.669 --> 00:05:02.300
So I'm going to look through my sales flow,
and the sales flow could be, you know, we

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:05.789
had a video that I did that's called the sales
process video -- why don't we put a picture?

00:05:05.789 --> 00:05:07.490
What's the title of that video?

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:09.099
How to improve your sales process?

00:05:09.099 --> 00:05:10.099
Something like that.

00:05:10.099 --> 00:05:11.931
Why don't we put the link here so they know
what it looks like?

00:05:11.931 --> 00:05:13.789
You can go find it.

00:05:13.789 --> 00:05:17.729
I look at that sales flow, the sales process,
on how I can improve it.

00:05:17.729 --> 00:05:19.659
Again, same exact thing.

00:05:19.659 --> 00:05:24.419
Score it 0-10, write down your good, bad,
ugly, and then your three actionable items.

00:05:24.419 --> 00:05:25.419
#3: Systems and Procedures

00:05:25.419 --> 00:05:28.889
The next one is systems and procedures.

00:05:28.889 --> 00:05:31.369
What is the system that we have in the company
for hiring?

00:05:31.369 --> 00:05:35.860
Meaning, when you sit down and you hire somebody,
what questions do you ask when hiring?

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:37.539
How was the firing protocol?

00:05:37.539 --> 00:05:38.629
How do we fire somebody?

00:05:38.629 --> 00:05:39.629
Who fires somebody?

00:05:39.629 --> 00:05:40.629
How is the exit interview?

00:05:40.629 --> 00:05:42.550
What do we do with the exit interview?

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:44.500
What opportunities do we give to them?

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.009
How do we let them go?

00:05:46.009 --> 00:05:48.990
What is the system when we have a complaint
come in?

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.289
What is the system that we have when we have
a question come in?

00:05:51.289 --> 00:05:54.240
What is the system that we have when we have
a good story come in?

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:58.649
What is the system and procedure that we have
when we recruit somebody that we're putting

00:05:58.649 --> 00:06:05.039
them in a department that's processing or
compliance or operations or . . . what is

00:06:05.039 --> 00:06:06.159
the system for them to learn?

00:06:06.159 --> 00:06:10.939
So if I bring a new hire, how is the new hire
going to learn about our company?

00:06:10.939 --> 00:06:13.229
How is the new hire going to be injected into
the culture?

00:06:13.229 --> 00:06:16.169
What process do they go through for orientation?

00:06:16.169 --> 00:06:19.659
Those are my systems and processes.

00:06:19.659 --> 00:06:24.629
Then the process comes down to areas on the
back end that I'm looking at with the processes

00:06:24.629 --> 00:06:27.870
and technology and the CRM, and is our CRM
doing a good job?

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:29.750
Can we get a better CRM?

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:31.330
How is the software that we're using?

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:32.490
Do we need to enhance the software?

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:35.009
What areas of the software are we not using
at all?

00:06:35.009 --> 00:06:39.039
So make a list of the 20 different areas in
the software that we use and which ones do

00:06:39.039 --> 00:06:40.309
we not use, rank them.

00:06:40.309 --> 00:06:41.780
Why do we have these things?

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:42.809
Why don't we eliminate them?

00:06:42.809 --> 00:06:44.210
What can we enhance?

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:47.999
These are all questions I'm asking about systems
and processes.

00:06:47.999 --> 00:06:52.750
Again, by the way, you're doing the exact
same thing here - scores 1-10, good, bad,

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:56.819
ugly, then your 1, 2, 3 actionable items,
tied to numbers and goals.

00:06:56.819 --> 00:06:57.819
#4: Partners

00:06:57.819 --> 00:06:58.819
Then it's partners.

00:06:58.819 --> 00:06:59.819
I write down partners.

00:06:59.819 --> 00:07:00.900
How are our partners doing?

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:05.439
Now keep in mind, I have partners here, and
I have vendors over here.

00:07:05.439 --> 00:07:06.539
Partners and vendors are different.

00:07:06.539 --> 00:07:12.610
A partner is somebody that I have worked with
generally for three years or more.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:18.129
Once somebody I've worked with for three years
or more who is invested in wanting to improve

00:07:18.129 --> 00:07:22.729
the relationship, they're investing money
and they're vested in wanting to improve the

00:07:22.729 --> 00:07:24.689
relationship, that becomes a partner to me.

00:07:24.689 --> 00:07:28.240
Then I'll ask, how's the partner doing with
us?

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.319
Are they servicing properly?

00:07:30.319 --> 00:07:31.560
Is it getting better?

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:33.479
What can we do to make this partnership better?

00:07:33.479 --> 00:07:37.619
So in the partnership category, I will make
a list of all of our partners.

00:07:37.619 --> 00:07:39.389
So let's just say it's five of them.

00:07:39.389 --> 00:07:40.419
How is this one doing?

00:07:40.419 --> 00:07:44.339
So the scoring on each one is going to be
different, because it's five partners.

00:07:44.339 --> 00:07:46.729
How's the good, bad, ugly of each partnership?

00:07:46.729 --> 00:07:50.270
What three actionable items do I have about
each partnership that I need to talk to them

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:52.529
when I have a conversation with them?

00:07:52.529 --> 00:07:56.949
So I put that together and then I'll say with
this partnership, have the numbers gone up?

00:07:56.949 --> 00:07:57.949
Has it gone down?

00:07:57.949 --> 00:07:58.949
Why has it gone down?

00:07:58.949 --> 00:07:59.949
Is it our fault?

00:07:59.949 --> 00:08:00.949
Is it their fault?

00:08:00.949 --> 00:08:02.409
What is it that their processes hasn't improved?

00:08:02.409 --> 00:08:05.479
What are some things they're maybe not happy
with us and we can improve and have we improved

00:08:05.479 --> 00:08:07.430
on it, and have we delivered on our promises?

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:12.059
I'm looking at that, with our partners, and
areas that my expectation of the partners.

00:08:12.059 --> 00:08:13.849
What do I need to go and negotiate with the
partners?

00:08:13.849 --> 00:08:15.810
What conversations do I need to have with
the partners?

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:20.550
I'm having those types of conversations and
writing them down, on which partners I need

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.370
to speak to again.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:24.139
That's the other area I inspect.

00:08:24.139 --> 00:08:26.559
#5: Customer Service

00:08:26.559 --> 00:08:29.389
How is our customer service?

00:08:29.389 --> 00:08:33.010
Is our customer service good or are we way
too aggressive?

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:34.270
Are we listening to the customers?

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:37.320
Do we become too offensive too early?

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:41.700
Is our way of selling a way that makes customers
happy?

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.310
What is the experience we're giving to our
customers?

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:45.590
What are the words that we're using?

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:48.019
Is it more of a script or is it more of an
experience?

00:08:48.019 --> 00:08:50.420
What is the difference between a customer
service and a customer experience?

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:54.710
Are we doing a good job teaching customer
experience and customer service?

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:59.020
Are we doing a good job taking care of our
clients in a way that we're getting more referrals?

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:05.550
So, I break that down, and I find out about
the five least happy clients that we had this

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:06.550
year.

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:07.750
Why were they not happy?

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:08.940
What did they do?

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:11.930
Out of the five, let's just say that one of
them was just a rant.

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:15.650
They were just unhappy, nothing made them
happy, and you can see the trend.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:18.360
Everybody is unhappy, everybody is unhappy
with that one client.

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:19.360
Great.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:20.500
But the other two had valid points.

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:22.520
And these other two had questions that we
never answered.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.590
Why don't we call these two?

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:25.750
Let's find out a little bit more.

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.990
Let's let them teach us about our customer
service.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:29.460
Tell us what you're not happy about.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:30.460
What happened?

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:31.460
We want to learn.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:32.460
We want to improve.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.460
Would you mind sharing that with us?

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:34.460
Yes, great.

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:36.450
And then giving them something just to share
their feedback with you.

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:37.550
Let's improve in this area.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:40.180
We've got to get better in this customer service
area.

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.510
We rank them and we try to improve that.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:45.860
This is probably one of the most important
ones and one of the most difficult ones because

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:49.690
it's an area you don't have control in, but
it's an area that when you're running and

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.750
gunning, you forget to do this sometimes.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:52.750
You need to do it.

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:53.830
The sooner you can do it, the better it is.

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:58.380
Again, same exact exercise, 1-10, good, bad,
ugly, three actionable items.

00:09:58.380 --> 00:09:59.820
#6: Brand

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:01.570
How's the brand doing?

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:03.240
What does the brand mean?

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:05.380
What does the market see our brand as?

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:06.650
Is it improving?

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:08.700
Is it getting into every single household?

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.550
What is the meaning of our brand?

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:12.400
What's the story behind our brand?

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.770
Tell me about the brand?

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:16.570
We sit down and say, "What do you think about
when you think about the company?"

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:18.680
If I were to ask you, "What do you think about
Valuetainment?"

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:19.950
what are things that would come to your mind?

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:21.700
What would you say about the brand Valuetainment?

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:22.880
What would you say?

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.370
You, would teach us.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:27.440
I would sit there in a meeting and say, "Guys,
what do you think about the company?

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:28.440
What does the company mean to you?

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.920
Can you tell me what our mission statement
means to you?"

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:32.300
And I want to see the heart.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.150
I don't want to see the logical side.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:35.740
I want to hear them.

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:38.190
Because based on their answer I'll realize,
man, we're too logical.

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:39.340
Why are we so logical?

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:43.130
Why do we get away from the initial mission
statement of the company?

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:44.570
Have we forgotten what it was all about?

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:47.300
Well maybe if we've forgotten what it was
all about, then it was my fault.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:50.020
I've got to take responsibility for it because
I'm the leader.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:51.050
What are we doing over here?

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:53.110
We've got to get better with the brand.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:57.790
So then the same thing with the brand - what
it means, breaking it down, going into it,

00:10:57.790 --> 00:11:01.790
looking at every aspect of the brand, looking
at everything with the website, social media,

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:08.090
all parts of it, then, same thing - score
1-10, good, bad, ugly, three actionable items

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:09.090
to improve in.

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:10.090
#7: Skills

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:11.970
Let me explain skills.

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:14.540
So skills for me is not just one dimensional.

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:15.970
Let me explain to you what I mean by skills.

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:22.780
So skills to me is first of all, most important
is me, how am I going to improve my skill

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:23.780
set?

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:24.780
How am I going to become a better CEO?

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:29.040
So for instance, I just went to Harvard Business
School, their OPM program, Owner President

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.040
and Management program.

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:33.370
I was with them for three weeks and I'm going
there next year and the following - it's a

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:34.370
three-year program.

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:38.060
And I'm around everybody in the room, net
worth, give or takes, 20 billion dollars combined,

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:43.360
with 144 of us, only 14 from America, 60 different
countries.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:44.360
So why go over there?

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:48.000
What skills do I need to improve in?

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:49.790
What areas do I need to improve in?

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:53.350
Do I need to get better at operations and
find somebody that's strong in operations?

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:55.190
Do I need to learn the ratios better?

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:57.440
Do I need to understand the finances better?

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:59.340
Do I need to understand development better?

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:01.570
Do I need to understand expansion better?

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:03.511
What are some areas I need to improve in?

00:12:03.511 --> 00:12:10.970
A lot of times the most challenging thing
with skills with you, the leader is, you think

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:13.040
you're good enough already.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.130
That's the biggest challenge I would say.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:16.270
You think you're already there.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:17.730
You think you've already arrived.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:21.850
You think you're already good enough to take
the company to the next level and you're not.

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:29.240
The Patrick that got his business to $100,000
a year revenue couldn't get the company to

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:31.250
a half a million dollars.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:32.970
He had to change and improve.

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:35.202
Then a half a million to a million he needs
to change, and a million to two million, and

00:12:35.202 --> 00:12:39.250
two million to five million and five million
to ten million, ten million to 20 million,

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:42.470
and 20 million to 50 million and 50 million
to 100 million - there is a part of recreating

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:43.470
yourself, right?

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:47.170
So skill set starts with myself, what I need
to improve in.

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:52.260
Then, my main executives and leaders - what
do they individually need to improve in?

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:56.970
So I'll take the skill sets of them, and really
assess it, and sometimes you don't like doing

00:12:56.970 --> 00:13:01.280
this, because it's time consuming, but one,
they will appreciate it so much that you put

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:04.750
time into it, two, the company's going to
grow.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:08.690
So if you think you're going to wing it, sometimes
people are blinded by their skills.

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:11.840
It requires coaching and a leader to say you
have a little bit of a thing here, you've

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:12.840
got to work on it.

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:14.470
This is not helping you in the business.

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:17.630
And the last time you had to work on this,
and you did, your income went up.

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:18.630
Your business grew.

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:19.630
You hit your goal.

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:21.220
So let's make sure we improve in this area.

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:26.390
So again, skill starts with me, then my main
core executives, then my customer service

00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:29.400
operations, what skills can we improve in?

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:32.590
Then, what area do we need to improve in on
the sales side?

00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:34.960
What area, and in every single thing it goes
skills.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.900
How to, how to, how to.

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:42.930
Then from that area, I either read the books
that we need to give and assign to those people,

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:49.690
an article, a video, a movie, a speaker, a
consultant, a keynote, it doesn't matter.

00:13:49.690 --> 00:13:51.030
We need to improve in audacity.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:53.200
We go bring somebody that's about audacity.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:55.280
For instance, we brought Grant Cardone.

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:58.190
We need to improve in seeing the vision about
capitalism.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.190
Boom!

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:00.950
We bring somebody that talks about capitalism.

00:14:00.950 --> 00:14:05.260
We need to improve entrepreneurship and seeing
that anybody can go from nothing to somebody.

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:06.840
Magic Johnson's a keynote speaker.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:11.040
We need to go and improve the area of management
and overcoming conflicts and all this other

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:12.040
stuff.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.040
Crucial conversations.

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:16.600
We need to figure out how to get better in
dealing with issues and systems.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:17.600
Let's go bring.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:18.850
. . it doesn't matter what it is.

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:23.210
We're constantly looking at skills that need
to improve, then figuring out tools to add

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.390
to improve this skill set.

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:28.510
So score, good, bad, ugly, 1, 2, 3 actionable
items.

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:29.980
#8: Expansion

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:35.290
Expansion is what market do you want to get
into that you're not into right now?

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:41.500
When we first started our insurance agency,
we were all in Northridge, California, one

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:42.960
office, 66 agents.

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:48.890
And we wanted to expand and grow from one
state to two states, so we went to Florida.

00:14:48.890 --> 00:14:49.890
Expansion.

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:51.910
I sent one of our executives over to Florida.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:56.140
And then from there, when Chad went to Florida,
working with John, then we said, how are we

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:57.140
going to go into different markets?

00:14:57.140 --> 00:15:01.610
Then we put our plan of action together, our
strategy together, on which markets we wanted

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:02.730
to get into.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:06.150
So then we put our plan of action together
and then all of a sudden, we went from two

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:11.590
states to five to ten, to 20, to 30, to 40
- I think we're in 44 or 45 states right now.

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:14.150
By the end of the year, we'll be in all states.

00:15:14.150 --> 00:15:16.550
But that's because we have to talk about expansion.

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:25.380
And I see a lot of times the entrepreneur
sometimes one, thinks about expansion too

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:32.589
early and loses the penetration that he has
locally, or they never think about it, and

00:15:32.589 --> 00:15:35.060
they just hope it happens accidentally.

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:40.521
Both ways there's a flaw, meaning, if you
have three people or five people or a small

00:15:40.521 --> 00:15:44.930
sales force, you don't want to all of a sudden
spread everybody thin and say you go over

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:46.089
here, you go over there.

00:15:46.089 --> 00:15:47.089
You're all of a sudden thin.

00:15:47.089 --> 00:15:48.089
It's like military.

00:15:48.089 --> 00:15:50.740
You don't want to go to war and tell your
generals you've got 200 soldiers, and you

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:56.500
tell 10 go here, 10 go there, 10 go here,
10 go there, and it's like 10 different soldiers

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:59.840
went 10 different places, and all of a sudden,
70 got killed because they're too weak, because

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:01.770
they faced 600 soldiers in one area.

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:03.710
You don't want to flank it like that.

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:11.540
So you go and expand and take your army from
100 to let's just say 350, then you move 50.

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:15.480
So you need to also know about expansion timing,
is it the right time for me to expand?

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:17.440
Is this person ready to go to a new market?

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:19.930
Are we ready to take this product into a new
market.

00:16:19.930 --> 00:16:21.320
Do we want to go into this state?

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:22.970
What are the top metropolitan cities?

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:28.270
Is our product tailored to a metropolitan
city or is our product tailored to a second

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:33.440
tier city that we want to get into that's
not maybe a top 20 metropolitan city.

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:34.440
What is it?

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:37.180
So you've got to sit there and really think
about expansion.

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.180
You've got to think about that.

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:42.080
Then again, same exact thing, 1-10, good,
bad, ugly, 3 actionable items.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:43.080
#9: Culture

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:44.490
Culture every single year.

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:51.270
So culture is something that it goes back
to the brand.

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:58.020
Brand and culture are very similar, but culture
sometimes the further you get away from it,

00:16:58.020 --> 00:17:02.400
and you no longer go circulate among the troops,
culture disappears.

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:07.129
It is very important for you to circulate
among your troops for the culture to stay

00:17:07.129 --> 00:17:08.129
intact.

00:17:08.129 --> 00:17:12.829
So I'm going to sit there and say, what was
the culture in the first year?

00:17:12.829 --> 00:17:14.389
What was the culture in the second year?

00:17:14.389 --> 00:17:16.010
What is the culture in the third year?

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.260
And we continue.

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:21.629
The basic thing I'll tell you is what is the
difference between a cult and a culture.

00:17:21.629 --> 00:17:23.169
Here's the difference.

00:17:23.169 --> 00:17:26.949
A cult is all predicated on a cult leader.

00:17:26.949 --> 00:17:31.590
A culture is no longer predicated on a cult
leader.

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:35.929
So maybe you went from being a cult, because
everything was dependent on you and you're

00:17:35.929 --> 00:17:38.230
no longer a cult, now you are a culture.

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:43.950
Because a cult leader can be disappearing
and the question is, if the cult leader dies,

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:46.240
will the culture continue?

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:50.740
And hopefully there's been duplication taking
place with other people taking the culture

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:55.950
to the next level where this is no longer
needed and it becomes a figure head or a voice,

00:17:55.950 --> 00:18:00.850
but the more you're touching the culture,
the thicker it gets and the more social capital

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:05.090
it creates, and then there's a part you're
talking are we evolving, are we adapting,

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:07.250
are we still the same?

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:11.970
Sometimes bigger companies, their problem
is their culture is a 50 culture, and you

00:18:11.970 --> 00:18:13.039
were still using DOS.

00:18:13.039 --> 00:18:14.039
We're old school with this.

00:18:14.039 --> 00:18:17.549
Well maybe old school doesn't work because
the person you're trying to attract is not

00:18:17.549 --> 00:18:18.690
turned on by old school.

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:20.799
So are you paying attention to that?

00:18:20.799 --> 00:18:21.799
So who do you want as a customer?

00:18:21.799 --> 00:18:25.350
Are they going to be interested in your culture
that hasn't adapted yet?

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:29.110
So the culture requires a lot of due diligence.

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:35.679
I did a video once, I think it's called 24
ways to build a company culture.

00:18:35.679 --> 00:18:39.600
Let's put a picture again, an image up here
again so you can see it on how to improve

00:18:39.600 --> 00:18:40.600
your culture.

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:44.600
And by the way, I get into very, very vivid
details on how I worked on the culture in

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:45.600
myself.

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:46.600
#10: Compliance

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:47.600
Boring.

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:48.600
No one likes compliance.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:50.309
This keeps you in business.

00:18:50.309 --> 00:18:51.889
Every business has compliance.

00:18:51.889 --> 00:18:54.080
you've got to get the best compliance people
working with you.

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:55.080
The best of them.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:19:00.509
Even when I was smaller and I was running
a sales shop out of the Granada Hills office

00:19:00.509 --> 00:19:03.880
and it was not the best area where we got
our office.

00:19:03.880 --> 00:19:05.900
A couple of times there was a drive by.

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:11.890
We had a legalized marijuana joint and they
were not only selling marijuana, they were

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:13.730
selling cocaine and other things out of this
place.

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:18.279
So anybody that would come into our office
would just smell the marijuana - maybe that's

00:19:18.279 --> 00:19:20.730
why people bought easily from us.

00:19:20.730 --> 00:19:22.539
Maybe that kind of helped out a little bit.

00:19:22.539 --> 00:19:29.549
But compliance was something I invested in,
because it kept me in business.

00:19:29.549 --> 00:19:32.649
Sometimes if you're the marketer and you're
a sales guy and you're going a million miles

00:19:32.649 --> 00:19:37.339
an hour and everything is sales, let's just
make it.

00:19:37.339 --> 00:19:42.950
. . and you're not hitting compliance, you're
all of a sudden creating an avalanche of compliance

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:46.990
problems that you need to put up with two
years from now that you could have solved

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:49.149
the sooner you touched up on compliance.

00:19:49.149 --> 00:19:50.610
So don't skip this too quickly.

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:55.149
This is very, very critical to know exactly
what compliance issues you have.

00:19:55.149 --> 00:19:57.519
Same exact exercise you need to do with compliance.

00:19:57.519 --> 00:20:00.119
And sometimes compliance will have to do with
hiring new team members.

00:20:00.119 --> 00:20:01.320
Keep that part in mind.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:02.759
#11: Vendors

00:20:02.759 --> 00:20:06.880
Vendors are people I'm doing business with,
that I'm transacting with.

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:12.080
I'm paying them, they're a vendor, and I'm
seeing which of these vendors can possibly

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:13.860
become partners.

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:16.100
And which of the vendors do I want to fire?

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:18.240
There's a vendor this year I'm firing.

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:20.259
I'm not happy with this vendor.

00:20:20.259 --> 00:20:23.830
That person's going to get a personal phone
call and "you're fired."

00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:28.950
Because I'm not happy with the way, sometimes
vendors, and I hope my vendors are watching

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:29.950
this, by the way.

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:33.179
You know who you are, because some of my partners
and vendors, some of you watch all of these

00:20:33.179 --> 00:20:35.850
videos and you message me afterwards.

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:39.009
If you're watching this vendors, I hope you're
seeing this.

00:20:39.009 --> 00:20:43.759
I love vendors who have aspirations of becoming
partners.

00:20:43.759 --> 00:20:47.830
I have a very big problem with vendors who
have already done business with you two or

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:51.129
three times and they've gotten 100, 200, 300
thousand dollars out of you, let's just say

00:20:51.129 --> 00:20:53.899
a million dollars out of you because you've
done business with them.

00:20:53.899 --> 00:21:01.340
So now they think it's on automatic that you're
going to say yes every single time and they

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:06.960
can now upsell you by 10% or 15% or in just
hidden commission stuff, because you're already

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:07.960
doing business with them.

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:09.999
I have a very big problem with that.

00:21:09.999 --> 00:21:12.340
And every time this has happened [snap], someone
gets fired.

00:21:12.340 --> 00:21:14.169
Every single time [snap] someone gets fired.

00:21:14.169 --> 00:21:18.140
So vendors I'm looking at which of them I
need to have a very private conversation with

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:21.070
them and tell them exactly what my expectation
of them is moving forward.

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:23.080
And I will have those conversations with vendors.

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:24.960
I will have those conversations with vendors.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:29.240
And then sometimes the vendors are doing such
a great job, I'm really hoping that we can

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:32.489
get over here [partners] and I tell them what
it's going to take to go from here [vendors]

00:21:32.489 --> 00:21:33.489
to here [partners].

00:21:33.489 --> 00:21:35.159
If we do this, then you become a partner.

00:21:35.159 --> 00:21:40.139
And when you become a partner, we endorse
you, and once we endorse you, everybody goes

00:21:40.139 --> 00:21:41.139
through you.

00:21:41.139 --> 00:21:43.749
And sometimes partners get demoted to vendors
as well.

00:21:43.749 --> 00:21:44.749
#12: Competition

00:21:44.749 --> 00:21:47.320
Last but not least is competition.

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:53.179
So competition may be what new competitors
are getting into the marketplace, what is

00:21:53.179 --> 00:21:59.110
the barrier to enter today, how are regulations
looking for us to go against the bigger guys?

00:21:59.110 --> 00:22:05.230
What bigger competitors are buying a presidential
campaign or nominee and funding them because

00:22:05.230 --> 00:22:10.049
they're hoping to add a new regulation or
law that's going to prevent us from competing

00:22:10.049 --> 00:22:11.049
with the bigger guys.

00:22:11.049 --> 00:22:12.289
I mean, we study all of this stuff.

00:22:12.289 --> 00:22:14.900
You know, you don't build a billion dollar
company accidentally.

00:22:14.900 --> 00:22:18.529
You need to know that these guys that are
up there, the bigger competitors don't want

00:22:18.529 --> 00:22:19.529
you to grow.

00:22:19.529 --> 00:22:20.649
They're wish is for you to go out of business.

00:22:20.649 --> 00:22:23.769
Listen, they're dreaming you'll go out of
business today.

00:22:23.769 --> 00:22:25.799
You know who you are, you're my competitor,
and you're watching this.

00:22:25.799 --> 00:22:28.020
Many of you watch, as my competitors.

00:22:28.020 --> 00:22:30.419
You are praying we go out of business today,
right?

00:22:30.419 --> 00:22:32.289
But we study you as well.

00:22:32.289 --> 00:22:35.549
We know how powerful you are, and sometimes
you've got to see who's coming up from here,

00:22:35.549 --> 00:22:41.970
who's getting down, who's getting out of the
game, who decided to get out of the certain

00:22:41.970 --> 00:22:45.239
product that you're in, they don't want to
touch it anymore, and why?

00:22:45.239 --> 00:22:47.080
What price are they being sold?

00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:50.529
What is the price point right now, kind of
like the comparables.

00:22:50.529 --> 00:22:55.440
What is the company's value because somebody's
company was sold for $17 billion so it automatically

00:22:55.440 --> 00:22:58.260
raises your valuation.

00:22:58.260 --> 00:23:01.900
All of those things you pay attention to with
competitors.

00:23:01.900 --> 00:23:04.409
Which one of them are calling you?

00:23:04.409 --> 00:23:06.299
Who wants to go from a competitor to a partner?

00:23:06.299 --> 00:23:09.639
Some of these competitors see you and say,
I don't want to compete with you, man.

00:23:09.639 --> 00:23:11.200
Can we become partners?

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:12.619
How can we become partners?

00:23:12.619 --> 00:23:16.940
Then you know there's possibly a relationship
there, so there's proper due diligence and

00:23:16.940 --> 00:23:17.940
investigation.

00:23:17.940 --> 00:23:20.929
It's pretty detailed here with the competition
side as well.

00:23:20.929 --> 00:23:21.929
And then boom.

00:23:21.929 --> 00:23:23.399
Same thing - numbers and goals.

00:23:23.399 --> 00:23:24.570
That you do.

00:23:24.570 --> 00:23:28.830
By the way, this, once a year takes a full
